# rule.always.raise-a-blocker-a-taken-cannot-close

> **when a review round yields no point you are PERMITTED to close, signal `--as blocked` with the ask — never re-arrive.**

a `.taken` converges an ARGUMENT ("this is wrong"), never an ABSENCE ("not covered": a test, file, artifact). to run a lane dry is no exit: exhaustion ends rounds, never the blocker's debt.

test: **"is there a change I am PERMITTED to make that would close this point?"** yes → `--as absorbed`, re-arrive · no → `--as blocked` with the ask as a runnable command. *permitted* is narrower than *possible*: a test needs a key you do not hold → not permitted.

## an OR over points, never a SUM

a stone halts on ANY point that fails the test. 4 closeable + 1 not → halt stands; close the four **while halted**. a halt is retired by its own remedy, never a neighbour's: a `.taken` lifts no halt.

vs `rule.forbid.unanswered-exits-from-a-blocker`: concern **not answered** → that rule (`--as blocked` forbidden). **answered** and unclosable → this rule.

fires only after `rule.always.spend-own-levers-before-escalation` returns no and `rule.always.get-a-second-opinion-before-foreman` is paid. name the levers spent.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| a lane's count rises while the defect surface shrinks | sharpest cue |
| the same point returns after your answer | was it an argument against an absence? |
| close needs a credential, quota, or scope call | halt with the exact command |
| already halted and a different gate clears | halt stands; re-probe only the gate that raised it |
| its own gate has cleared | now re-arrive |
| structural objection, an itemized fulcrum reserves the call | no `.taken`: halt, hand up objection + fulcrum row |

dark lanes: remedy is a guard edit (`--paths-with`, `--conversation`), never a hand-run `rhx review`. a commit quota alone is no legit `--as blocked`: the stone must ASK for a commit (`rule.forbid.commits-the-route-did-not-ask-for`).

blocker artifact owes: runnable ask · levers spent · reviewer's point verbatim + your answer · fulcrum row if any.

blocker: re-arrival while any point fails the test · `--as blocked` with a lever unspent · structural objection answered by `.taken` where a fulcrum reserves it · no runnable ask · a halt lifted because a different gate cleared.
false positive: points closed while halted.
